From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alessandro Fontana <alessandro.fontana@pm.me>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 19:15:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] thermal: Subscribe to events after setting ops

The LibThermal constructor calls thermal_init() before the Thermal
constructor sets the event callbacks. thermal_events_init() only
subscribes to the events whose callbacks are set, so every thermal
event was dropped and no status change was ever reported.

Initialize the events again once the callbacks are set.

Assisted-by: LLM
Change-Id: I8413b366219f26c64020977fe6f53c0f4a719ce4
---
 hal/thermal/src/Thermal.cpp | 13 +++++++------
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/hal/thermal/src/Thermal.cpp b/hal/thermal/src/Thermal.cpp
index 93ef41d..10207ee 100644
--- a/hal/thermal/src/Thermal.cpp
+++ b/hal/thermal/src/Thermal.cpp
@@ -790,12 +790,9 @@ Thermal::Thermal(Looper *looper)
 	}
 
 	/*
-	 * The Thermal class is inherited from the LibThermal. The
-	 * constructor of the Libthermal will initialize itself. We
-	 * can safely set the callback after the initialization of the
-	 * LibThermal as those are needed when calling the
-	 * 'thermal_events_handle()' function, so after setting and
-	 * polling the file descriptor.
+	 * The LibThermal constructor ran thermal_init() with empty ops, and
+	 * thermal_events_init() only subscribes to events whose callbacks are
+	 * set: set them, then initialize the events again below.
 	 */
         m_ops.events.tz_create   = thermalZoneCreate;
 	m_ops.events.tz_delete   = thermalZoneDelete;
@@ -811,6 +808,10 @@ Thermal::Thermal(Looper *looper)
 	m_ops.events.cdev_update = cdevUpdate;
 	m_ops.events.gov_change  = govChange;
 
+	thermal_events_exit(this->m_th);
+	if (thermal_events_init(this->m_th))
+		throw("Failed to initialize the thermal events");
+
 	if (!looper->addFd(thermal_events_fd(this->m_th), 0,
 			   Looper::EVENT_INPUT, thermalHandleEvent, this))
 		throw("Failed to add thermal file descriptor to the mainloop");
